From ef4dbefd3c7fa9e272c8a1730f307c460c88a0b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 11:53:16 +0545
Subject: [PATCH] Retire additional purchase bills from the bill screen and API

Customs, excise and similar charges are recorded with an import cost
assessment, and an agent's or freight invoice is a service bill linked to
the goods bill, so a separate additional bill is redundant.

- Bill screen: remove "Add Charges", the "Additional to Bill" field and
  every additional-bill branch; the term picker for a bill is now limited
  to the GENERAL category (it used to list ADDITIONAL terms on normal bills
  and the server then refused the save).
- API: POST/PUT /bills answer 400 (field mainBillId) when mainBillId is set.
- Service and database rules are unchanged, so any additional bill that
  already exists can still be viewed, posted and reversed.
- Tests: assessment test builds its legacy additional bills through the
  service; the API test now checks the 400 and that nothing is stored.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UJ94HWDZsmypsV2sVkB9bn
